IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ppl-logic`
IMPORT `ppl-time`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425, Chapter 2 Part 2-1 (sections 7 to 11D): the key provisions.
-- Section 7 is a guide to the Part and states no rule of its own.
-- Section 11D (what a flexible PPL day is) is in ppl-time, with the counting of the second birthday.
-- A bar ("cannot ... unless") answers JUST FALSE when it applies and NOTHING when it does not: the text does not say the Secretary can.

-- src:368 | Parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child if a determination of the Secretary that parental leave pay is payable to the person for that day is in force under section 13 or 14.
@ref s 11A (src:368-368)
GIVEN `a determination of the Secretary that parental leave pay is payable to the person for that day is in force under section 13 or 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day` MEANS
    JUST `a determination of the Secretary that parental leave pay is payable to the person for that day is in force under section 13 or 14`

-- src:371 | The Secretary cannot make a determination under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child unless the person was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on that day.
@ref s 11B (src:371-371)
GIVEN `the person was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a determination under section 13 or 14 for a flexible PPL day, as section 11B bears on it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person was or will be eligible for parental leave pay on the day`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:374 | The Secretary cannot make a determination under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person for a flexible PPL day for a child unless the person has made:
-- src:375 | (a) an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day (in which case the person is a PPL claimant); or
-- src:376 | (b) an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day (in which case the person is a special PPL claimant).
@ref s 11C (src:374-376)
GIVEN `the person has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Secretary can make a determination under section 13 or 14 for a flexible PPL day, as section 11C bears on it` MEANS
    IF `the person has made an effective PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day` OR `the person has made an effective special PPL claim for parental leave pay for that day`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE
